d:idSpecObject_-880013300_10
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.775(d).Amendment 18;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(d) The design of windshields and windows in pressurised aeroplanes must be based on factors peculiar to high altitude operation, including the effects of continuous and cyclic pressurisation loadings, the inherent characteristics of the material used, and the effects of temperatures and temperature differentials. The windshield and window panels must be capable of withstanding the maximum cabin pressure differential loads combined with critical aerodynamic pressure and temperature effects after any single failure in the installation or associated systems. It may be assumed that, after a single failure that is obvious to the flight crew (established under CS 25.1523), the cabin pressure differential is reduced from the maximum, in accordance with appropriate operating limitations, to allow continued safe flight of the aeroplane with a cabin pressure altitude of not more than 4572m (15 000 ft) (see AMC 25.775(d)).</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "775" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(d)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Windshields and windows" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 18;" ;
	o:idSection1 "SUBPART D – DESIGN AND CONSTRUCTION" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "PERSONNEL AND CARGO ACCOMMODATIONS" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-10066" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2016/010/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2016-06-24T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2016-06-24T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_-880013300_11
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.775(e).Amendment 18;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(e) The windshield panels in front of the pilots must be arranged so that, assuming the loss of vision through any one panel, one or more panels remain available for use by a pilot seated at a pilot station to permit continued safe flight and landing.</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
