d:idSpecObject_-1182953428_11
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.1093(b)(2).Amendment 18;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(2) Idle for a minimum of 30 minutes on the ground in the following icing conditions shown in Table 1 below, unless replaced by similar test conditions that are more critical. These conditions must be demonstrated with the available air bleed for icing protection at its critical condition, without adverse effect, followed by an acceleration to take-off power or thrust, in accordance with the procedures defined in the aeroplane flight manual. During the idle operation the engine may be run up periodically to a moderate power or thrust setting in a manner acceptable to the Agency. The applicant must document the engine run-up procedure (including the maximum time interval between run-ups from idle, run-up power setting, and duration at power), the associated minimum ambient temperature, if any, and the maximum time interval. These conditions must be used in the analysis that establishes the aeroplane operating limitations in accordance with CS 25.1521. (See AMC 25.1093(b)) Table 1- Icing conditions for ground tests </div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "1093" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(b)(2)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Air intake system de-icing and anti-icing provisions" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 18;" ;
	o:idSection1 "SUBPART E – POWERPLANT" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "AIR INTAKE SYSTEM" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-10135" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
