d:idSpecObject_-304003163_9
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.1401(e).Initial issue;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(e) Light intensity. The minimum light intensities in all vertical planes, measured with the red filter (if used) and expressed in terms of ‘effective’ intensities, must meet the requirements of sub-paragraph (f) of this paragraph. The following relation must be assumed: <object data=\"images/CS-25_27_-304003163-10.jpg\" type=\"image/jpg\"></object> where: Ie = effective intensity (candela (candles) I(t) = instantaneous intensity as a function of time t2–t1 = flash time interval (seconds) Normally, the maximum value of effective intensity is obtained when t2 and t1 are chosen so that the effective intensity is equal to the instantaneous intensity at t2 and t1. </div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
