d:idSpecObject_-1342275228_root
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.1447.Amendment 19;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(See AMC 25.1447)If oxygen-dispensing units are installed, the following apply: </div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "1447" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Equipment standards for oxygen dispensing units" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 19;" ;
	o:idSection1 "SUBPART F – EQUIPMENT" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "MISCELLANEOUS EQUIPMENT" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-10196" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2017/015/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idReqIfChapterName1 "CS 25.1447.Amendment 19;" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2017-05-16T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2017-05-16T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_-1342275228_5
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.1447(a).Amendment 19;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(a) There must be an individual dispensing unit for each occupant for whom supplemental oxygen is to be supplied. Units must be designed to cover the nose and mouth and must be equipped with a suitable means to retain the unit in position on the face. Flight crew masks for supplemental oxygen must have provisions for the use of communication equipment.</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "1447" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(a)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Equipment standards for oxygen dispensing units" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 19;" ;
	o:idSection1 "SUBPART F – EQUIPMENT" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "MISCELLANEOUS EQUIPMENT" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-10196" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2017/015/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2017-05-16T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2017-05-16T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_-1342275228_6
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.1447(b).Amendment 19;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(b) If certification for operation up to and including 7620 m (25 000 ft) is requested, an oxygen supply terminal and unit of oxygen dispensing equipment for the immediate use of oxygen by each crew member must be within easy reach of that crew member. For any other occupants the supply terminals and dispensing equipment must be located to allow use of oxygen as required by the operating rules.</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "1447" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(b)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Equipment standards for oxygen dispensing units" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 19;" ;
	o:idSection1 "SUBPART F – EQUIPMENT" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "MISCELLANEOUS EQUIPMENT" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-10196" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2017/015/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2017-05-16T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2017-05-16T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_-1342275228_7
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.1447(c).Amendment 19;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(c) If certification for operation above 7620 m (25 000 ft) is requested, there must be oxygen dispensing equipment meeting the following requirements (See AMC 25.1447(c)):</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "1447" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(c)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Equipment standards for oxygen dispensing units" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 19;" ;
	o:idSection1 "SUBPART F – EQUIPMENT" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "MISCELLANEOUS EQUIPMENT" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-10196" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2017/015/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2017-05-16T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2017-05-16T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_-1342275228_8
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.1447(c)(1).Amendment 19;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(1) There must be an oxygen-dispensing unit connected to oxygen supply terminals immediately available to each occupant, wherever seated. If certification for operation above 9144 m (30 000 ft) is requested, the dispensing units providing the required oxygen flow must be automatically presented to the occupants before the cabin pressure altitude exceeds 4572 m (15 000 ft) and the crew must be provided with a manual means to make the dispensing units immediately available in the event of failure of the automatic system. The total number of dispensing units and outlets must exceed the number of seats by at least 10%. The extra units must be as uniformly distributed throughout the cabin as practicable. (See AMC 25.1447(c)(1).)</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "1447" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(c)(1)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Equipment standards for oxygen dispensing units" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 19;" ;
	o:idSection1 "SUBPART F – EQUIPMENT" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "MISCELLANEOUS EQUIPMENT" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-10196" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2017/015/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2017-05-16T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2017-05-16T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_-1342275228_9
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.1447(c)(2).Amendment 19;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(2) Each flight-crew member on flight deck duty must be provided with demand equipment. In addition, each flight-crew member must be provided with a quick-donning type of oxygen dispensing unit, connected to an oxygen supply terminal, that is immediately available to him when seated at his station, and this is designed and installed so that it (see AMC 25.1447(c)(2)) –</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "1447" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(c)(2)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Equipment standards for oxygen dispensing units" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 19;" ;
	o:idSection1 "SUBPART F – EQUIPMENT" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "MISCELLANEOUS EQUIPMENT" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-10196" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2017/015/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2017-05-16T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2017-05-16T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_-1342275228_10
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.1447(c)(2)(i).Amendment 19;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(i) Can be placed on the face from its ready position, properly secured, sealed, and supplying oxygen upon demand, with one hand within 5 seconds and without disturbing eyeglasses or causing delay in proceeding with emergency duties; and</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
