d:idSpecObject_1805953230_17
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx C Part II(d)(5).Amendment 16;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(5) Crew activation of the ice protection system is in accordance with a normal operating procedure provided in the Aeroplane Flight Manual, except that after beginning the takeoff roll, it must be assumed that the crew takes no action to activate the ice protection system until the airplane is at least 122 m (400 ft) above the takeoff surface.</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx C Part II" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(d)(5)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Airframe Ice Accretions" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 16;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix C" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-10005" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2015/008/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2015-03-13T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2015-03-13T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_1805953230_18
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx C Part II(e).Amendment 16;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(e) The ice accretion before the ice protection system has been activated and is performing its intended function is the critical ice accretion formed on the unprotected and normally protected surfaces before activation and effective operation of the ice protection system in continuous maximum atmospheric icing conditions. This ice accretion only applies in showing compliance to CS 25.143(j), 25.207(h) and 25.207(i). <object data=\"images/CS-25_27_image91.png\" type=\"image/png\"></object> FIGURE 1 CONTINUOUS MAXIMUM (STRATIFORM CLOUDS) ATMOSPHERIC ICING CONDITIONS LIQUID WATER CONTENT VS MEAN EFFECTIVE DROP DIAMETER Source of data – NACA TN No. 1855, Class III –M, Continuous Maximum. <object xmlns:reqif-xhtml=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" data=\"images/CS-25_27_image92.png\" type=\"image/png\"></object> FIGURE 2 CONTINUOUS MAXIMUM (STRATIFORM CLOUDS) ATMOSPHERIC ICING CONDITIONS AMBIENT TEMPERATURE VS PRESSURE ALTITUDE Source of data – NACA TN No. 2569. <object xmlns:reqif-xhtml=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" data=\"images/CS-25_27_image93.png\" type=\"image/png\"></object> FIGURE 3 CONTINUOUS MAXIMUM (STRATIFORM CLOUDS) ATMOSPHERIC ICING CONDITIONS LIQUID WATER CONTENT FACTOR VS CLOUD HORIZONTAL DISTANCE Source of data – NACA TN No. 2738. <object xmlns:reqif-xhtml=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" data=\"images/CS-25_27_image94.png\" type=\"image/png\"></object> FIGURE 4 INTERMITTENT MAXIMUM (CUMULIFORM CLOUDS) ATMOSPHERIC ICING CONDITIONS LIQUID WATER CONTENT VS MEAN EFFECTIVE DROP DIAMETER Source of data – NACA TN No. 1855, Class II – M, Intermittent Maximum <object xmlns:reqif-xhtml=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" data=\"images/CS-25_27_image95.png\" type=\"image/png\"></object> FIGURE 5 INTERMITTENT MAXIMUM (CUMULIFORM CLOUDS) ATMOSPHERIC ICING CONDITIONS AMBIENT TEMPERATURE VS PRESSURE ALTITUDE Source of data – NACA TN No. 2569. <object xmlns:reqif-xhtml=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" data=\"images/CS-25_27_image96.png\" type=\"image/png\"></object> FIGURE 6 INTERMITTENT MAXIMUM (CUMULIFORM CLOUDS) ATMOSPHERIC ICING CONDITIONS VARIATION OF LIQUID WATER CONTENT FACTOR WITH CLOUD HORIZONTAL EXTENT Source of data – NACA TN No. 2738.</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx C Part II" ;
