	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2009/010/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_-1302882791_64
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx F Part VI(e)(1).Amendment 6;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(1) With the sliding platform out of the chamber, install the calorimeter holding frame. Push the platform back into the chamber and insert the calorimeter into the first hole (‘‘zero’’ position). See figure 7. Close the bottom door located below the sliding platform. The distance from the centerline of the calorimeter to the radiant panel surface at this point must be 191 ± 3 mm (7½ ± ⅛ inches). Prior to igniting the radiant panel, ensure that the calorimeter face is clean and that there is water running through the calorimeter. </div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx F Part VI" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(e)(1)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Test Method to Determine the Flammability and Flame Propagation Characteristics of Thermal/Acoustic Insulation Materials" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 6;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix F" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-9589" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2009/010/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_-1302882791_65
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx F Part VI(e)(2).Amendment 6;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(2) Ignite the panel. Adjust the fuel/air mixture to achieve 1.7 Watts/cm2 ± 5% (1.5 BTUs/ft2 sec ± 5%) at the ‘‘zero’’ position. If using an electric panel, set the power controller to achieve the proper heat flux. Allow the unit to reach steady state (this may take up to 1 hour). The pilot burner must be off and in the down position during this time. </div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx F Part VI" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(e)(2)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Test Method to Determine the Flammability and Flame Propagation Characteristics of Thermal/Acoustic Insulation Materials" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 6;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix F" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-9589" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2009/010/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_-1302882791_66
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx F Part VI(e)(3).Amendment 6;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(3) After steady-state conditions have been reached, move the calorimeter 51 mm (2 inches) from the ‘‘zero’’ position (first hole) to position 1 and record the heat flux. Move the calorimeter to position 2 and record the heat flux. Allow enough time at each position for the calorimeter to stabilize. Table 1 depicts typical calibration values at the three positions. TABLE 1.—CALIBRATION TABLE </div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx F Part VI" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(e)(3)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Test Method to Determine the Flammability and Flame Propagation Characteristics of Thermal/Acoustic Insulation Materials" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 6;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix F" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-9589" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2009/010/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_-1302882791_68
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx F Part VI(e)(4).Amendment 6;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(4) Open the bottom door. Remove the calorimeter and holder fixture. Use caution as the fixture is very hot. </div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
