d:idSpecObject_1862917770_root
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx I 2.Initial issue;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx I 2" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Definitions" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Initial issue;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix I – Automatic Takeoff Thrust Control System (ATTCS)" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-8670" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2003/2/RM" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idReqIfChapterName1 "CS 25.Apdx I 2.Initial issue;" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2003-10-17T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2003-10-17T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_1862917770_3
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx I 2(a).Initial issue;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(a) AutomaticTakeoff Thrust Control System (ATTCS). An ATTCS system is defined as a system which automatically resets thrust or power on the operating engine(s) when any engine fails during take-off. For the purpose of the requirements in this Appendix, the ATTCS system comprises all elements of equipment necessary for the control and performance of each intended function, including all devices both mechanical and electrical that sense engine failure, transmit signals and actuate fuel controls or power levers of the operating engine(s) to achieve scheduled thrust or power increases, the engine control system and devices which furnish cockpit information on system operation. </div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx I 2" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(a)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Definitions" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Initial issue;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix I – Automatic Takeoff Thrust Control System (ATTCS)" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-8670" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2003/2/RM" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2003-10-17T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2003-10-17T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_1862917770_4
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx I 2(b).Initial issue;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(b) Critical Time Interval. When conducting an ATTCS take-off, the critical time interval is between one second before reaching V1, and the point on the gross take-off flight path with all engines operating where, assuming a simultaneous engine and ATTCS system failure, the resulting flight path thereafter intersects the gross flight path, determined in accordance with CS 25.115, at not less than 122 m (400 feet) above the take-off surface. This definition is shown in the following figure:</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx I 2" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(b)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Definitions" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Initial issue;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix I – Automatic Takeoff Thrust Control System (ATTCS)" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-8670" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2003/2/RM" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2003-10-17T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2003-10-17T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_1586589071_root
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx I 3.Initial issue;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">All applicable performance requirements of CS-25 must be met with the ATTCS system functioning normally as designed, except that the propulsive thrust obtained from each operating engine after failure of the critical engine during take-off, and the thrust at which compliance with the one-engine-inoperative climb requirements in CS 25.121(a) and (b) is shown, must be assumed to be not greater than the lesser of – </div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx I 3" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Performance requirements" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Initial issue;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix I – Automatic Takeoff Thrust Control System (ATTCS)" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-8674" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2003/2/RM" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idReqIfChapterName1 "CS 25.Apdx I 3.Initial issue;" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2003-10-17T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2003-10-17T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_1586589071_4
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx I 3(a).Initial issue;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(a) The actual propulsive thrust resulting from the initial setting of power or thrust controls with the ATTCS system functioning normally as designed, without requiring any action by the crew to increase thrust or power until the aeroplane has achieved a height of 122 m (400 feet) above the take-off surface; or</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx I 3" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(a)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Performance requirements" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Initial issue;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix I – Automatic Takeoff Thrust Control System (ATTCS)" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-8674" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2003/2/RM" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2003-10-17T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2003-10-17T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_1586589071_5
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx I 3(b).Initial issue;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(b) 111 percent of the propulsive thrust which would have been available at the initial setting of power or thrust controls in the event of failure of the ATTCS system to reset thrust or power, without any action by the crew to increase thrust or power until the aeroplane has achieved a height of 122 m (400 feet) above the take-off surface. Note 1. The limitation of performance credit for ATTCS system operation to 111 percent of the thrust provided at the initial setting is intended to:</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx I 3" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(b)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Performance requirements" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Initial issue;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix I – Automatic Takeoff Thrust Control System (ATTCS)" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-8674" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2003/2/RM" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2003-10-17T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2003-10-17T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_1586589071_7
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx I 3(b)(i).Initial issue;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(i) Assure an adequate level of climb performance with all engines operating at the initial setting of power or thrust controls, and </div>" ;
