d:idSpecObject_1552261622_38
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx O Part I(c).Amendment 16;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(c) Horizontal extent The liquid water content for freezing drizzle and freezing rain conditions for horizontal extents other than the standard 32.2 km (17.4 nautical miles) can be determined by the value of the liquid water content determined from Figure 1 or Figure 4, multiplied by the factor provided in Figure 7, which is defined by the following equation: S = 1.266 – 0.213 log10(H) Where S = Liquid Water Content Scale Factor (dimensionless) and H = horizontal extent in nautical miles Figure 7 – Appendix O, Horizontal Extent, Freezing Drizzle and Freezing Rain <object data=\"images/CS-25_27_image138.png\" type=\"image/png\"></object></div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
