d:idSpecObject_-520380064_root
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "AMC 25.1447(c)(2).Initial issue;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">AMC 25.1447(c)(2) Equipment standards for oxygen dispensing units ED Decision 2003/2/RM Unless it is required that the pilot at the control is wearing his mask and breathing oxygen while the altitude exceeds 7620 m (25 000 feet), the design of the flight-crew masks and their stowages should be such that each mask can be placed in position and put into operation in not more than five seconds, one hand only being used, and will thereafter remain in position, both hands being free. </div>" ;
