d:idSpecObject_-1439567751_9
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.253(a)(3).Amendment 18;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(3) With the aeroplane trimmed at any speed up to VMO/MMO, there must be no reversal of the response to control input about any axis at any speed up to VDF/MDF. Any tendency to pitch, roll, or yaw must be mild and readily controllable, using normal piloting techniques. When the aeroplane is trimmed at VMO/MMO, the slope of the elevator control force versus speed curve need not be stable at speeds greater than VFC/MFC, but there must be a push force at all speeds up to VDF/MDF and there must be no sudden or excessive reduction of elevator control force as VDF/MDF is reached.</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
