	rdfs:label "CS 25.809(b)(3).Amendment 17;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(3) Even though persons may be crowded against the door on the inside of the aeroplane.</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "809" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(b)(3)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Emergency exit arrangement" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 17;" ;
	o:idSection1 "SUBPART D – DESIGN AND CONSTRUCTION" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "EMERGENCY PROVISIONS" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-10040" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2015/019/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2015-07-17T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2015-07-17T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_1047426119_7
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.809(b).Amendment 17;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(b) Each emergency exit must be openable from the inside and the outside except that sliding window emergency exits in the flight crew area need not be openable from the outside if other approved exits are convenient and readily accessible to the flight crew area. Inward opening doors may be used if there are means to prevent occupants from crowding against the door to an extent that would interfere with the opening of the door. Each emergency exit must be capable of being opened, when there is no fuselage deformation –</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "809" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(b)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Emergency exit arrangement" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 17;" ;
	o:idSection1 "SUBPART D – DESIGN AND CONSTRUCTION" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "EMERGENCY PROVISIONS" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-10040" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2015/019/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2015-07-17T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2015-07-17T00:00:00Z" ;
	cas:lists d:idSpecObject_1047426119_8 ,
		d:idSpecObject_1047426119_9 ,
		d:idSpecObject_1047426119_10 .

d:idSpecObject_1047426119_11
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.809(c).Amendment 17;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(c) The means of opening emergency exits must be simple and obvious and may not require exceptional effort; and must be arranged and marked so that it can be readily located and operated, even in darkness. Internal exit opening means involving sequence operations (such as operation of two handles or latches or the release of safety catches) may be used for flight crew emergency exits if it can be reasonably established that these means are simple and obvious to crewmembers trained in their use.</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "809" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(c)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Emergency exit arrangement" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 17;" ;
	o:idSection1 "SUBPART D – DESIGN AND CONSTRUCTION" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "EMERGENCY PROVISIONS" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-10040" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2015/019/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2015-07-17T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2015-07-17T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_1047426119_12
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.809(d).Amendment 17;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(d) If a single power-boost or single power-operated system is the primary system for operating more than one exit in an emergency, each exit must be capable of meeting the requirements of sub-paragraph (b) of this paragraph in the event of failure of the primary system. Manual operation of the exit (after failure of the primary system) is acceptable.</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "809" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(d)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Emergency exit arrangement" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 17;" ;
	o:idSection1 "SUBPART D – DESIGN AND CONSTRUCTION" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "EMERGENCY PROVISIONS" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-10040" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2015/019/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2015-07-17T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2015-07-17T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_1047426119_13
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.809(e).Amendment 17;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(e) Each emergency exit must be shown by tests, or by a combination of analysis and tests, to meet the requirements of sub-paragraphs (b) and (c) of this paragraph.</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
