d:idSpecObject_-1777977512_12
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.1325(d).Amendment 16;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(d) Each pressure altimeter must be approved and must be calibrated to indicate pressure altitude in a standard atmosphere, with a minimum practicable calibration error when the corresponding static pressures are applied.</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "1325" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(d)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Static pressure systems" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 16;" ;
	o:idSection1 "SUBPART F – EQUIPMENT" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "INSTRUMENTS: INSTALLATION" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-9996" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2015/008/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2015-03-13T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2015-03-13T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_-1777977512_13
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.1325(e).Amendment 16;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(e) Each system must be designed and installed so that the error in indicated pressure altitude, at sea-level, with a standard atmosphere, excluding instrument calibration error, does not result in an error of more than ±9 m (±30 ft) per 185 km/hr (100 knots) speed for the appropriate configuration in the speed range between 1·23 VSR0 with wing-flaps extended and 1·7 VSR1 with wing-flaps retracted. However, the error need not be less than ±9 m (±30 ft).</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "1325" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(e)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Static pressure systems" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 16;" ;
	o:idSection1 "SUBPART F – EQUIPMENT" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "INSTRUMENTS: INSTALLATION" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-9996" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2015/008/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2015-03-13T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2015-03-13T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_-1777977512_14
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.1325(f).Amendment 16;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(f) If an altimeter system is fitted with a device that provides corrections to the altimeter indication, the device must be designed and installed in such manner that it can be bypassed when it malfunctions, unless an alternate altimeter system is provided. Each correction device must be fitted with a means for indicating the occurrence of reasonably probable malfunctions, including power failure, to the flight crew. The indicating means must be effective for any cockpit lighting condition likely to occur.</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
