d:idSpecObject_-1302882791_30
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx F Part VI(b)(4).Amendment 6;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(4) Pilot Burner. The pilot burner used to ignite the specimen must be a BernzomaticTM (or equivalent) commercial propane venturi torch with an axially symmetric burner tip and a propane supply tube with an orifice diameter of 0.15 mm (0.006 inches). The length of the burner tube must be 71 mm (2⅞ inches). The propane flow must be adjusted via gas pressure through an in-line regulator to produce a blue inner cone length of 19 mm (¾ inch) . A 19 mm (¾ inch) guide (such as a thin strip of metal) may be soldered to the top of the burner to aid in setting the flame height. The overall flame length must be approximately 127 mm (5 inches) long. Provide a way to move the burner out of the ignition position so that the flame is horizontal and at least 50 mm (2 inches) above the specimen plane. See figure 6. <object data=\"images/CS-25_27_image117.jpeg\" type=\"image/jpeg\"></object></div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx F Part VI" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(b)(4)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Test Method to Determine the Flammability and Flame Propagation Characteristics of Thermal/Acoustic Insulation Materials" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 6;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix F" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-9589" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2009/010/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_-1302882791_33
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx F Part VI(b)(5).Amendment 6;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(5) Thermocouples. Install a 24 American Wire Gauge (AWG) Type K (Chromel-Alumel) thermocouple in the test chamber for temperature monitoring. Insert it into the chamber through a small hole drilled through the back of the chamber. Place the thermocouple so that it extends 279 mm (11 inches) out from the back of the chamber wall, 292 mm (11½ inches) from the right side of the chamber wall, and is 51 mm (2 inches) below the radiant panel. The use of other thermocouples is optional.</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
