d:idSpecObject_-1302882791_59
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx F Part VI(c)(1).Amendment 6;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(1) Specimen preparation. Prepare and test a minimum of three test specimens. If an oriented film cover material is used, prepare and test both the warp and fill directions. </div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx F Part VI" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(c)(1)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Test Method to Determine the Flammability and Flame Propagation Characteristics of Thermal/Acoustic Insulation Materials" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 6;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix F" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-9589" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2009/010/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_-1302882791_60
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx F Part VI(c)(2).Amendment 6;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(2) Construction. Test specimens must include all materials used in construction of the insulation (including batting, film, scrim, tape etc.). Cut a piece of core material such as foam or fiberglass, and cut a piece of film cover material (if used) large enough to cover the core material. Heat sealing is the preferred method of preparing fiberglass samples, since they can be made without compressing the fiberglass (‘‘box sample’’). Cover materials that are not heat sealable may be stapled, sewn, or taped as long as the cover material is over-cut enough to be drawn down the sides without compressing the core material. The fastening means should be as continuous as possible along the length of the seams. The specimen thickness must be of the same thickness as installed in the airplane. </div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx F Part VI" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(c)(2)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Test Method to Determine the Flammability and Flame Propagation Characteristics of Thermal/Acoustic Insulation Materials" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 6;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix F" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-9589" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2009/010/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_-1302882791_61
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx F Part VI(c)(3).Amendment 6;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(3) Specimen Dimensions. To facilitate proper placement of specimens in the sliding platform housing, cut non-rigid core materials, such as fibreglass, 318 mm (12½ inches) wide by 584 mm (23 inches) long. Cut rigid materials, such as foam, 292 ± 6 mm (11½ ± ¼ inches) wide by 584 mm (23 inches) long in order to fit properly in the sliding platform housing and provide a flat, exposed surface equal to the opening in the housing. </div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
