d:idSpecObject_2060306491_4_zero
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx N 4(a)(0).Amendment 6;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(a) Atmospheric Ambient Temperatures and Fuel Properties. </div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx N 4" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(a)(0)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Variables and data tables  " ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 6;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix N – Fuel Tank Flammability ExposureED Decision 2016/010/R(See )" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-9596" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2009/010/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idParentIR1 "Appendix N – Fuel Tank Flammability Exposure" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_2060306491_5
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx N 4(a)(1).Amendment 6;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(1) In order to predict flammability exposure during a given flight, the variation of ground ambient temperatures, cruise ambient temperatures, and a method to compute the transition from ground to cruise and back again must be used. The variation of the ground and cruise ambient temperatures and the flash point of the fuel is defined by a Gaussian curve, given by the 50 percent value and a 1-standard deviation value. </div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx N 4" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(a)(1)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Variables and data tables  " ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 6;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix N – Fuel Tank Flammability ExposureED Decision 2016/010/R(See )" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-9596" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2009/010/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idParentIR1 "Appendix N – Fuel Tank Flammability Exposure" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_2060306491_6
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx N 4(a)(2).Amendment 6;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(2) Ambient Temperature: Under the program, the ground and cruise ambient temperatures are linked by a set of assumptions on the atmosphere. The temperature varies with altitude following the International Standard Atmosphere (ISA) rate of change from the ground ambient temperature until the cruise temperature for the flight is reached. Above this altitude, the ambient temperature is fixed at the cruise ambient temperature. This results in a variation in the upper atmospheric temperature. For cold days, an inversion is applied up to 10,000 feet, and then the ISA rate of change is used. </div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx N 4" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(a)(2)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Variables and data tables  " ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 6;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix N – Fuel Tank Flammability ExposureED Decision 2016/010/R(See )" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-9596" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2009/010/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idParentIR1 "Appendix N – Fuel Tank Flammability Exposure" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_2060306491_8
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx N 4(a)(3)(i).Amendment 6;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(i) For Jet A and Jet A-1 fuel, the variation of flash point of the fuel is defined by a Gaussian curve, given by the 50 percent value and a 1-standard deviation, as shown in Table 1.</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx N 4" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(a)(3)(i)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Variables and data tables  " ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 6;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix N – Fuel Tank Flammability ExposureED Decision 2016/010/R(See )" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-9596" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2009/010/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idParentIR1 "Appendix N – Fuel Tank Flammability Exposure" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_2060306491_10
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx N 4(a)(3)(ii)(A).Amendment 6;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(A) LFL at sea level = flash point temperature of the fuel at sea level minus 5.5°C (10F). LFL decreases from sea level value with increasing altitude at a rate of 0.55 °C (1oF) per 808 feet.</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx N 4" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(a)(3)(ii)(A)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Variables and data tables  " ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 6;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix N – Fuel Tank Flammability ExposureED Decision 2016/010/R(See )" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-9596" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2009/010/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idParentIR1 "Appendix N – Fuel Tank Flammability Exposure" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_2060306491_11
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx N 4(a)(3)(ii)(B).Amendment 6;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(B) UFL at sea level = flash point temperature of the fuel at sea level plus 19.5°C (63.5oF). UFL decreases from the sea level value with increasing altitude at a rate of 0.55°C (1oF) per 512 feet.</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx N 4" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(a)(3)(ii)(B)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Variables and data tables  " ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 6;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix N – Fuel Tank Flammability ExposureED Decision 2016/010/R(See )" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-9596" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2009/010/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idParentIR1 "Appendix N – Fuel Tank Flammability Exposure" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2009-07-06T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_2060306491_9
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx N 4(a)(3)(ii).Amendment 6;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(ii) The flammability envelope of the fuel that must be used for the flammability exposure analysis is a function of the flash point of the fuel selected by the Monte Carlo for a given flight. The flammability envelope for the fuel is defined by the upper flammability limit (UFL) and lower flammability limit (LFL) as follows:</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx N 4" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(a)(3)(ii)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Variables and data tables  " ;
