	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(6) Altitude and temperature envelope: Figure 3 – Appendix O, Freezing Drizzle, Altitude and Temperature <object data=\"images/CS-25_27_image134.png\" type=\"image/png\"></object> (b) Freezing Rain (Conditions with spectra maximum drop diameters greater than 500 μm): (1) Pressure altitude range: 0 to 3656 m (12000 ft) MSL. (2) Maximum vertical extent: 2134 m (7000 ft). (3) Horizontal extent: standard distance of 32.2 km (17.4 nautical miles). (4) Total liquid water content: Note: LWC in grams per cubic meter (g/m3) based on horizontal extent standard distance of 32.2 km (17.4 nautical miles). Figure 4 – Appendix O, Freezing Rain, Liquid Water Content <object xmlns:reqif-xhtml=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" data=\"images/CS-25_27_image135.png\" type=\"image/png\"></object></div>" ;
