d:idSpecObject_198645633_51
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx O Part II(d).Amendment 16;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(d) The ice accretion before the ice protection system has been activated and is performing its intended function is the critical ice accretion formed on the unprotected and normally protected surfaces before activation and effective operation of the ice protection system in the icing conditions defined in part I of this appendix. This ice accretion only applies in showing compliance to CS 25.143(j) and 25.207(h).</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx O Part II" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(d)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Airframe ice accretions" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 16;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix O – Supercooled Large Drop icing conditionsED Decision 2015/008/RAppendix O consists of two parts. Part I defines Appendix O as a description of supercooled large drop (SLD) icing conditions in which the drop median volume diameter (MVD) is less than or greater than 40 μm, the maximum mean effective drop diameter (MED) of Appendix C continuous maximum (stratiform clouds) icing conditions. For Appendix O, SLD icing conditions consist of freezing drizzle and freezing rain occurring in and/or below stratiform clouds. Part II defines ice accretions used to show compliance with CS-25 specifications.[Amdt 25/16]" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-9991" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2015/008/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idParentIR1 "Appendix O – Supercooled Large Drop icing conditions" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2015-03-13T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2015-03-13T00:00:00Z" .

d:idSpecObject_198645633_52
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "CS 25.Apdx O Part II(e).Amendment 16;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">(e) In order to reduce the number of ice accretions to be considered when demonstrating compliance with the requirements of CS 25.21(g), any of the ice accretions defined in this appendix may be used for any other flight phase if it is shown to be at least as critical as the specific ice accretion defined for that flight phase. Configuration differences and their effects on ice accretions must be taken into account.</div>" ;
	dcterms:modified "2026-02-24T16:47:22.4536074+01:00"^^xs:dateTime ;
	o:idType1 "Requirement" ;
	o:idLabel1 "CS 25" ;
	o:idRef1 "Apdx O Part II" ;
	o:idSubref1 "(e)" ;
	o:idTitle1 "Airframe ice accretions" ;
	o:idAmendedBy1 "Amendment 16;" ;
	o:idSection1 "APPENDICES TO CS-25" ;
	o:idSubsection1 "Appendix O – Supercooled Large Drop icing conditionsED Decision 2015/008/RAppendix O consists of two parts. Part I defines Appendix O as a description of supercooled large drop (SLD) icing conditions in which the drop median volume diameter (MVD) is less than or greater than 40 μm, the maximum mean effective drop diameter (MED) of Appendix C continuous maximum (stratiform clouds) icing conditions. For Appendix O, SLD icing conditions consist of freezing drizzle and freezing rain occurring in and/or below stratiform clouds. Part II defines ice accretions used to show compliance with CS-25 specifications.[Amdt 25/16]" ;
	o:ideRules1 "ERULES-1963177438-9991" ;
	SpecIF:Domain "Initial airworthiness;" ;
	o:idRegulatorySource1 "ED Decision 2015/008/R" ;
	o:idRegulatorySubject1 "CS-25;" ;
	o:idTypeOfContent1 "CS (Certification specification);" ;
	o:idParentIR1 "Appendix O – Supercooled Large Drop icing conditions" ;
	o:idApplicabilityDate1 "2015-03-13T00:00:00Z" ;
	o:idEntryIntoForceDate1 "2015-03-13T00:00:00Z" .

