d:idSpecObject_-1893283893_root
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "AMC 25.812(e)(2).Amendment 19;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">AMC 25.812(e)(2) Emergency lighting ED Decision 2017/015/R If it is desired to identify each emergency exit by means of a symbolic sign, this sign should be white and green in compliance with European Standard (EN) ISO 7010:2012, Graphical symbols, safety colours and safety signs, registered safety signs. Example of an acceptable design of symbolic sign to identify an exit The direction of the ‘running man’ (to the left/to the right) should not suggest movement away from the emergency exit. The type of signs used to identify an emergency exit (letter based, symbolic) should be chosen to be consistent with the emergency exit signs throughout the cabin. [Amdt 25/3] [Amdt 25/19]</div>" ;
