d:idSpecObject_1700076396_root
	a o:idSpecObject1 ;
	rdfs:label "AMC 25.1310(a).Initial issue;" ;
	rdfs:comment "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">AMC 25.1310(a) Power source capacity and distribution ED Decision 2003/2/RM When alternative or multiplication of systems and equipment is provided to meet the requirements of CS 25.1310(a), the segregation between circuits should be such as to minimise the risk of a single occurrence causing multiple failures of circuits or power supplies of the system concerned. For example, electrical cable bundles or groups of hydraulic pipes should be so segregated as to prevent damage to the main and alternative systems and power supplies.</div>" ;
